On Sat, 21 Feb 2015 16:07:54 +0100, Thomas Petazzoni wrote:

> Like the last two years, we have registered Buildroot as a potential
> organization for the Google Summer of Code 2015. Of course, we don't
> know if Google will accept our application.
> 
> That being said, while this process is going on, we have started a Wiki
> page to collect ideas of projects:
> 
>   http://elinux.org/Buildroot:GSoC_2015_Ideas

Sadly, Google rejected our application for the GSoC 2015, so we will
not have any GSoC project this year. We asked the reason of the
rejection, and they said that it was due to the fact that 1/ they had a
record number of applications this year and 2/ our ideas page was too
short in details.

